# Testing

**When:** adding or fixing `*_test.go`, handler/store tests, or choosing unit vs integration.

Default suite must not require real Postgres, real outbound network, or a running `taskapi`.

---

## Pattern

```go
func TestUserService_Create(t *testing.T) {
    tests := []struct {
        name    string
        input   CreateUserInput
        mock    func(*mockUserStore)
        wantErr error
    }{
        {
            name:  "valid user",
            input: CreateUserInput{Email: "a@b.com"},
            mock:  func(m *mockUserStore) { m.On("Create", mock.Anything, mock.Anything).Return(nil) },
        },
        {
            name:    "duplicate email",
            input:   CreateUserInput{Email: "a@b.com"},
            mock:    func(m *mockUserStore) { m.On("Create", mock.Anything, mock.Anything).Return(domain.ErrConflict) },
            wantErr: domain.ErrConflict,
        },
    }

    for _, tt := range tests {
        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {
            store := &mockUserStore{}
            tt.mock(store)
            svc := NewUserService(store)
            _, err := svc.Create(context.Background(), tt.input)
            if !errors.Is(err, tt.wantErr) {
                t.Errorf("got %v, want %v", err, tt.wantErr)
            }
        })
    }
}
```

---

## Layers

| Layer | What | Tools |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Unit | Service/domain logic, mocks | fast, no I/O |
| Integration | Store vs sqlite/test DB | `internal/tasktestdb/`, build tags when needed |
| Handler | HTTP surface | `httptest.NewRecorder` / `NewServer` |
| E2E | Thin smoke against a running env | sparingly |

---

## Rules

- Test **behavior**, not private implementation details.
- Every test independent — no shared mutable state, no ordering deps.
- `t.Parallel()` in unit tests when safe; integration: `t.Cleanup`.
- Files: `foo_test.go`; heavy integration: `foo_integration_test.go` + build tag.
- Always `t.Run` for table rows.
- Always cover error paths.
- Prefer existing helpers (`internal/tasktestdb/`, `internal/handlertest/`).
- Prefer `testify` when neighbors already use it.
- Oversized test files: extract fixtures/builders — never copy production logic into tests.

---

## Do not

- Depend on execution order or package-level mutable fixtures.
- Hit real external network or production DB in default CI tests.
